course: dictionary
lesson: 12819
title: Embrace: hug, welcome or include
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Embrace can be a verb or a noun. As a verb, it means to put your arms around someone, or to welcome something happily. As a noun, an embrace is a hug.
explain: «She gave her grandma a warm embrace at the station.» The word warm and the arms around her tell you it is a hug. Ask: what word would fit here? Hug fits, so embrace means hug.
explain: «Mia decided to embrace the new challenge.» A challenge cannot be hugged, so here embrace means to accept it happily and with enthusiasm.
explain: In formal writing, embrace can mean to include. «The club embraces children of all ages.» The clue is all ages: the club takes in every age, so embrace means include.
fact: Embrace is a verb and a noun: we embrace each other, or we give an embrace.
fact: «Embrace» means to hold someone in your arms to show love or friendship.
fact: «Embrace» can also mean to accept a change or idea happily.
fact: In formal writing, «embrace» means to include or contain.
fact: A good check is to swap in hug, welcome or include and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The twins ran across the field and shared a happy embrace.» What is an embrace here? | A loud shout | A kind of football game | A race | *A hug
exercise: «Sam was nervous, but he chose to embrace the new school.» What does embrace mean here? | Run away from | Paint | *Welcome happily | Forget
exercise: «The library embraces books from every country.» What does embraces mean here? | Keeps only one | Sells cheap | Throws away | *Includes
test: «Dad gave me a warm embrace before bed.» What does embrace mean? | *A hug | A bedroom | A bad dream | A cold drink
test: «Lena likes to embrace change and try new things.» What does embrace mean? | Measure | *Welcome happily | Hide from | Sleep through
exam: «The festival embraces music, dance and art.» What does embraces mean? | Forgets | Hurts | Rushes past | *Includes
